<title>USA: Meadowbrook sees slight accretion from deal.</title>
<headline>Meadowbrook sees slight accretion from deal.</headline>
<dateline>SOUTHFIELD, Mich. 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Meadowbrook Insurance Group Inc said it expects its acquisition of Crest Finance Corp will be &quot;slightly&quot; accretive to earnings in 1997.</p>
<p>Meadowbrook said it completed the previously announced acquisition of 100 percent of the common and preferred stock of Crest Financial for $8.7 million in cash. Crest is a California-based, full service insurance operation specializing in truck insurance.</p>
<p>Meadowbrook is an alternative risk management company. Its insurance subsidiaries include Star Insurance Co and Savers Property and Casualty Insurance Co.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
